WEBVTT

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:05.430
Twenty-nine.

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:08.490
Thirty.

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:10.650
Done with today's reps!

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:20.790
<b>Naruse Naoko</b> 
Can I talk to you?

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:22.790
Naruse-san?

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:26.240
I guess if you look at it like this,

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:32.790
I've made a lot.

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:37.390
You're going to make something really 
wonderful and put it up in the café, right?

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:43.490
None of these feel like they're "it."

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:48.270
None feels right.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:50.080
Huh?

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:54.230
Touko-senpai?

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:58.450
Thank you for bringing Arai-san 
to our place today.

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:03.450
Thank you for bringing Arai-san 
to our place today. 

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:08.950
That... is... fine! Send.

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:44.010
<b>Beyond the Calm Autumn Sky</b>

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:49.020
<b><i>Nagase</i></b>

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.750
Touko-senpai!

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:55.570
Senpai!

00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:59.090
You didn't have to run.

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:04.550
But you said... there was something... you wanted 
me to eat... before we go to the café.

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:07.350
Wait, is it in that bag?

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:10.840
Oh, no. We're here for 
limited-time sweets from that shop.

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:15.380
Sorry I couldn't talk to you 
properly yesterday.

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:16.790
Oh, not at all!

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:19.330
I was able to pick up a 
lot of valuable things.

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:23.390
But how come you have that big bag with you?

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:24.850
So you're curious?

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:27.050
I'm super curious!

00:03:27.050 --> 00:03:28.200
I thought so.

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:31.080
So what is it?

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:42.360
Wow! That's so... how should I put it...

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:45.900
It's bold! It really catches your eye.

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:46.940
Right?

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:49.090
It looks really expensive.

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:54.000
It wasn't that expensive, but it's a piece 
that I've been looking at for a long time.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.800
I spent all my saved up 
New Year's money to buy this.

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:02.760
When I sent Mika-chan a photo of it 
last night, she called me right away.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:04.070
She was so surprised.

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:06.210
I can see why!

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:09.930
When I put it up in my 
room, I got all excited.

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:13.490
It's know it's a bit silly, but it 
made me feel kind of invincible!

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.880
I can understand why.

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:21.020
Wow, this gets me excited too!

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:21.990
Right?

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:25.110
I'm not even sure how to start eating this.

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:28.870
It's so good!

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:32.950
I've told you before, but you 
know my grandpa is a potter.

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:36.710
My father has started selling his works,

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:39.260
and my mother's family have worked
 as potters for generations as well.

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:42.010
You've really grew up surrounded by pottery.

00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:44.140
I have.

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:47.810
That's why I naturally came to love pottery.

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:57.220
I made a lot and got a lot of praise, 
which made me love it even more.

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:02.080
But I wonder when it happened...

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:07.190
When pottery became 
something I had to do properly...

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:11.260
Everybody around me expected it,

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:14.250
and I convinced myself that
I should be able to do it as well.

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:21.380
Once I got into middle school, 
I always got a fever before contests.

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:23.060
You did?

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:25.490
My grandpa was just too great,

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:27.940
and I didn't realize how much 
pressure that put on me.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:31.610
Pressure, huh?

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:37.280
I was just doing it to feel like 
a person worthy of my grandpa,

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:40.040
then they made me the president of the 
student council in middle school.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:43.020
In turn, that amplified my feelings

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:46.990
that everyone was expecting me 
to do something amazing.

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:49.740
We're back!

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:57.030
But then, in the second 
year of middle school,

00:05:57.030 --> 00:06:00.420
I had the urge to use red, a color 
my grandfather hardly ever used.

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:05.260
When I proudly went to show 
him my first piece...

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:08.710
I'm sorry, I'm really busy now,

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:11.010
so please don't come to 
the workshop anymore.

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:17.530
That made me think, "Oh, I guess
I have to make things his way..."

00:06:17.930 --> 00:06:19.390
Oh, no...

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:23.330
But that's not what it was.

00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:28.000
Yesterday, after you left,

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:31.370
my grandfather asked me to go 
with him to the Eihouji Temple.

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:46.300
For about two hours, we only walked.

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:51.360
When I tried to talk to him, 
all he'd say back was "yeah" or "uh-huh."

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:57.800
But then, while I was in awe of the fall leaves 
in the middle of the Musai Bridge...

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:02.910
They're so beautiful.

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:05.000
Yeah.

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:16.580
The blue of summer is good, 
but the bright red of fall is good, too.

00:07:17.110 --> 00:07:17.800
Yes.

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:21.380
I guess you don't get it.

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:22.280
Huh?

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:26.210
Of course you wouldn't.

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:31.450
Since I was embarrassed, I asked 
your teacher to not tell you,

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:33.960
but I saw your new plate.

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:37.220
What?

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:42.510
I'm sorry I always kept you at arm's length.

00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:46.900
Kouzou and Nanako both understand 
how hard this profession can be.

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:49.930
They were probably worried about you.

00:07:50.350 --> 00:07:53.280
They asked me to not give 
too much attention to you.

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:55.730
My mom and dad said to do that?

00:07:56.970 --> 00:07:59.050
Since I'm not so good at this,

00:07:59.050 --> 00:08:02.220
I couldn't help but fawn over you 
when you came to the workshop.

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:07.000
Since you were at that age,

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:10.030
they told me you'd lose interest 
if we left you alone.

00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:19.300
I was so happy to see you continue.

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:26.010
That red sure is beautiful.

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:30.660
Those gold brush strokes are wonderful, too.

00:08:31.450 --> 00:08:33.120
You mean my big plate?

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:38.030
It was the first thing you've 
made that made me truly jealous.

00:08:41.210 --> 00:08:43.360
Do you understand?

00:08:44.820 --> 00:08:45.640
Yes!

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:49.760
Don't worry about what I like.

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:53.300
Just make the things you want 
to make, the way you like.

00:08:54.990 --> 00:08:58.630
I am me, and you are you.

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:07.040
Grandpa...

00:09:10.350 --> 00:09:11.610
Thank you!

00:09:16.050 --> 00:09:17.190
Why...

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:19.190
I don't know why...

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:23.800
I'm sorry, I don't know why...

00:09:25.470 --> 00:09:28.400
Because you're in the 
same boat, Toyokawa-san.

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:32.130
Your mother, Tokikawa Himena, is a legend.

00:09:32.810 --> 00:09:35.250
Aren't you feeling that pressure?

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:41.210
That's the shelf where
 your best piece will go, right?

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:44.520
Why?

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:47.860
Last night, Naruse-san sent me a message.

00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:49.540
Nao-chan did?

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:53.650
She said that she thinks you're 
too preoccupied with that shelf.

00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:57.640
Your mother would say the 
same thing, I think.

00:09:57.990 --> 00:10:00.970
She'd tell you to not worry so much
 and to just make what you like.

00:10:04.090 --> 00:10:08.450
Mom, if you were still alive,
 what would you say?

00:10:11.300 --> 00:10:13.500
I'm just going to give it my best!

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:16.060
But don't laugh if it ends up
 being kinda weird!

00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:24.170
I wonder if my careless idea 
ended up hurting Himeno.

00:10:24.170 --> 00:10:26.090
I think it'll be fine.

00:10:26.090 --> 00:10:28.680
That girl probably understands.

00:10:28.680 --> 00:10:31.760
That spot is not for comparing,

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:34.100
it's for having them side by side.

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:42.660
<b>Beauty Salon Naruse</b>

00:10:37.060 --> 00:10:39.690
Uh, despite your very busy schedule,

00:10:39.690 --> 00:10:42.660
thank you for... No, that's not it.

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:47.400
Aoki-senpai, thank you for all that 
you've done for our Himeno...

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:50.480
No, that's not it, either.

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:53.620
Aw heck, I'll just jump in!

00:10:58.240 --> 00:10:59.270
<i>Hello?</i>

00:10:59.270 --> 00:11:02.130
May I please speak to Aoki-senpai?

00:11:02.130 --> 00:11:03.970
<i>What's going on, Naruse-san?</i>

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:08.640
I, well, I just got a thank-you
 message from Hime-chan.

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:10.180
It seems her head is clear now,

00:11:10.180 --> 00:11:12.450
so I really wanted to thank you for that!

00:11:12.450 --> 00:11:13.920
<i>I'm glad to hear that.</i>

00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:16.830
<i>You didn't have to call for that, though.</i>

00:11:16.830 --> 00:11:19.530
No, this time, I wanted to do it right.

00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:21.430
Thank you so much!

00:11:21.430 --> 00:11:23.910
Then, I will be.. Yes. Yes.

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:25.920
Excuse me.

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:39.540
I'm so tired.

00:11:58.170 --> 00:11:59.740
And then!

00:12:01.210 --> 00:12:03.580
Hime-chan, you're here too early!

00:12:08.470 --> 00:12:10.500
Oh, nice!

00:12:10.990 --> 00:12:12.580
Can I take a video?

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:15.830
Eh? I guess.

00:12:18.180 --> 00:12:20.340
I liked Hime-chan's expression.

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:22.340
Me, too.

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:25.600
Yours, too.

00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:26.520
Huh?

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:34.850
So, Hime-chan!

00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:40.340
Thank you!

00:12:40.340 --> 00:12:42.400
Huh? For what?

00:12:43.440 --> 00:12:44.790
I wonder.

00:12:44.790 --> 00:12:46.270
What?

00:12:46.270 --> 00:12:47.970
I won't tell you!

00:12:47.360 --> 00:12:49.790
Hey, come on!

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:50.960
Never.

00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:52.380
Hey!

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:55.110
Stop!

00:12:57.820 --> 00:12:59.770
Tell me!

00:14:25.250 --> 00:14:27.110
Seeing the Mexico girl again.

00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:35.310
<b>Mini-Mini Pottery Club</b>

00:14:27.110 --> 00:14:28.720
A moment with the reserved girl.

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:30.730
A word from the adviser.

00:14:30.730 --> 00:14:33.940
All of which are treasures 
for the bob-haired girl!

00:14:33.940 --> 00:14:35.910
Next Episode: "Found It!"

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:39.970
<b>Next Time:</b>

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:39.970
<b>Found It!</b>

00:14:35.910 --> 00:14:39.600
Today's connection and 
encounters were so good.
